  "description": "The Eiffel artifact creation event (ID\u202f123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000) of type\u202fEiffelArtifactCreatedEvent, version\u202f3.0.0, was recorded at Unix time\u202f1728467200. It is tagged as \u201cartifact\u201d and \u201ccreation\u201d. The source of the event is the build system at buildsystem.company.com (domain\u202fmy-domain), identified by the name \u201cartifactCreator\u201d, serialized with pkg:json, and reachable via\u202fhttps://buildsystem.company.com/artifacts/123e4567. Security details list the author as john.doe@example.com; the integrity protection uses an RS256 signature\u202fdGVzdHNpZ25hdHVyZQ==\u202fwith the public key\u202fMIIBIjANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQEFAAOCAQ8AMIIBCgKCAQEAv..., and the event participates in the \u201cartifact\u2011sequence\u201d at position\u202f42.  \n\nThe artifact itself is identified as\u202fpkg:com.example.myartifact and is named \u201cMy Artifact\u201d. Its file set includes \u201cbuild.gradle\u201d (tagged \u201cbuild\u201d and \u201cgradle\u201d) and \u201cREADME.md\u201d. The build command used was \u201cmake all\u201d, and the artifact requires an implementation of type\u202fANY. It depends on the packages\u202fpkg:com.example.library1\u202fand\u202fpkg:com.example.library2, and it implements\u202fpkg:com.example.interface1. A custom data entry records the release level as \u201cbeta\u201d. Finally, this event is linked with a CAUSE relationship to the event\u202f9f8e7d6c-5b4a-3c2d-8e0f-9a8b7c6d5e4f.",
